The consensus seem to be to increase time_t to 64 bits. This will keep
the current semantics of time_t (0 = 1/1/1970 etc.) but this breaks
backward binary compatibilty. Some vendors have already implemented 64
bit time_t in their new 64 bit OS's (Sun & HP). Compaq has not done his
yet but I suspect and suggest they will bump it up to 64 bits - I would
prefer in DU 5.0, but I think they are concerned with binary
compatibilty...

