In article <6s1g8p$lk0$1@nnrp1.dejanews.com>,
 <heitbaum@my-dejanews.com> wrote:
> I am having the following problem with a multithreaded application compiled
> with GNU C++ under DU4.0d. I have read the FAQ page, and know what the
> problem is but does any one have a suggestion on how to track this down.
> 
> Unaligned access pid=7579 <darxStoreServer> va=0x3ff800dd634 pc=0x120022a64
> ra=0x120022a40 inst=0x8c220000
> Segmentation fault      (core dumped)

Rudi-

I believe the FAQ mentions an approach you can take.  Essentially, you use
`uac' to change the default unaligned access behavior from one of just `print'
to one that also causes a bus error signal to be delivered.  Then just run
your application under a debugger like gdb or ladebug.  When the unaligned
access occurs, the debugger should catch the signal and you should be able
to pin down where the unaligned access is coming from.

Tim
