Hi,

I am sitting here for planning a new (digital unix) network with a lot
of workstations, and - of course :) - one or more servers.
Now i am thinking about if it would be better to build workstations that
can run for them alone ("a full installation") and connect them to the
network via NIS,NFS and so on, or if it would be better to use (true)
cluster technology.

A good thing of the second idea would be that os- updates only had to
done on ONE machine, and installing new software/ scripts also would be
easier. But what about the traffic the clustertechnology produces in
the net, and other possibly disadvantages ?

If someone in this newsgroup already thought about this questions (and
got a result...), or knows the URL of such a comparison, a should note
(with cc: to me, please) would be nice !

Regards,
Philipp Pallo.



