According to Joerg Lippmann  <jlippmann@ifm.uni-kiel.de>:
-->
-->Hi!
-->
-->Is there an easy way to read sun binary data files with DEC-Alpha
-->f77-programs?
-->
-->J�rg
-->

Yes. set an environment variable FORT_CONVERTnn to "BIG_ENDIAN",
where nn is the logical unit number in fortran used to read 
(or write) the file, before running your program. You can use
as many nn's as needed. This does depend on the program reading
the data into the correct data type. 

