>Solaris 2.6 <-> Digital Unix 4.0 workstations we have here,
>even with a carefully patched Solaris 2.6 (patch list see below).
>The Solaris 2.6 clients nearly hang during excessive NFS writes.

How is performance with UDP?  We have an issue with TCP vs. the
small window size Solaris and others use on TCP connections.  I've only
seen the problem with 32 KB writes (not yet supported in released
code), but it might be a problem with 8KB I/O too.  If so, mounting
with a wsize of 4096 might avoid that problem (and open other
performance problems).

There's another really weird problem that was involved NFS v2 and
data cache invalidation when doing writes to a fast server. We
developed a patch (800 lines of code!) for a 3rd party vendor.
As far as I know, NFS V3 didn't have a problem, but since V2 was
in use, it may have predated Sun's V3 support.
