You are hiding the c-library function by your repeated declaration of 
mknod before the main. At least you should use an extern "C" {} if you 
require such a hack for some reason. The c++ compiler will then not 
mangle the types into the function name and give the linker a chance to 
find the function name in the c-library... 
btw: the c compiler warns because the signature is not ok, the second argument is mode_t which is a typedef from unsigned int. 

The following works fine for me:

23:43 margay_sts:~> cat mknod.cc
#include <sys/stat.h>
int main(){
  mknod("foo", S_IFIFO |0666, 0);
}
23:43 margay_sts:~> cxx -D_XOPEN_SOURCE_EXTENDED mknod.cc
23:44 margay_sts:~> a.out
23:44 margay_sts:~> ls -l foo
prw-r--r--   1 sts      cron           0 Aug 25 23:44 foo|

