------
Digital UNIX does not use print filters in a remote lpd print environment.
You will need to preformat the file prior to printing. I can post a shell
script if you need one.

If you are printing to a network printer and are using Digital UNIX V4.0a
or later switch to tcp/ip printing.  Tcp/ip printing provides full printing
functionality including the use of print filters and the generation of
banner pages. This is documented either in the release notes or in the
system admin guide.  If necessary I can also post a brief description on
how to setup the environment.

If you provid more detailed information such as the version of UNIX, the
printer make and model, and how it is connected, I may be able to provide
additional information.

Regards,
Ernest LaBonte

