Its like Ernest say, like most lpr systems. The old trick is  to  get  a
input  filter to work is to use a _local_ dummy printer /dev/null in the
/etc/printcap. Then the lpd runs the input filter ...

Use a filter  programm  (/usr/local/daemon/filter/if_a2ps  below)  which
catchs stdin and reformat it and send it to the remote printer (raw).

ps|a2ps:\
        :if=/usr/local/daemon/filter/if_a2ps:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lperr:\
        :lp=/dev/null:\
        :mx#0:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd/a2ps:\

raw|lp1|unix:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lperr:\
        :lp=:\
        :rm=pcubXX.ub.uni-marburg.de:\
        :rp=unix:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd/raw:\
        :sh:\
        :mx#0:

A minifilter

#!/bin/sh
cat - | lpr -Praw

Hope this helps

	Juergen



