Your workstation wouldn't happen to have a ZLXp-E3 card in it, would it?
I've seen this phenomenon with that particular card, and I've been told
by a very knowledgeable person from Digital (thanks Pat!) that it's a
problem with the ZLXp-E3.

This generally only happens when you start X -- once the pointer's visible
it will stay visible until the next time you exit X completely and need to
restart.  If you power the workstation off and let it cool for a while,
the pointer will probably be visible again.

