Hi.

We are having some trouble running slirp on our AlphaServer 1000, OSF
4.0.  We have two Practical Peripherals 56K modems, connected to
/dev/tty00 and /dev/tty01.  We built slirp without problems, and it
sort of runs, i.e. it doesn't dump core or suchlike.

The problem we see is that only a few packets get through.  Using the
telnet connection to slirp, "stats ip" shows that about half the
packets are listed as ``with length too short (len < sizeof(iphdr))''.
The total number of packets is also quite small (e.g. 50 in each
direction after a few minutes of trying to use netscape or telnet).
Typically, telnet or netscape from the slirp client to some host will
simply hang until the request times out.  We are able to run slirp
thru an rlogin to a different host (which is not an Alpha) from the
one to which the modems are attached.  This works quite well.

I suspect a timing or handshaking problem.  The inittab entry for a
modem line looks like this:

modem0:34:respawn:/usr/sbin/getty /dev/tty00 M57600 vt100

The gettydefs definition for the modem is

M57600# B57600 HUPCL CS8 # B57600 SANE CRTSCTS IXANY TAB3 HUPCL #%h %t login: #M38400

The modem itself is set to factory defaults except for things not
relevant to communication, like answer on 1 ring and speaker off.  It
generally connects using v4.2bis and LAPM protocols.

Any suggestions for a cure?

Thanks,

