Paul Chapin wrote:
> 
> Is there a way to run dxaccounts without it locking the password file.  It
> takes almost ten minutes to load so I don't want to have to start it
> everytime I want to check an account.

10 minutes? What do you have? It usually takes less than 10 seconds for me.

> Or, is there a way to check the lock status of an account without using
> dxaccounts.  I can set the status using usermod, but I'd like to be able to
> check and see if that's the user's problem first.

Use "edauth" command. It displays a selected entry from a specified security
database. See man pages, but I think it would be something like:

edauth -g -d p <user_name>

If you see "...:u_lock:..." field, then it's administratively locked.
If it's not there or it says "...:@u_lock:..." then it's OK.
If there was an excessive failed login case, then ther would be
"...:failures#<n>:..."

Nix.





