> 
> I am trying to dial in to my DEC AlphaStation 500 (V4.0b) and establish
> a ppp connection.  I have done this on several other unix systems with
> no problem.  I have tried every getty I could find, played with the pppd
> options...no luck.  Has anyone successfully done this?  Digital's
> documentation on this is scant at best.  I would appreciate any help you
> can offer.

"Network administration" - "PPP setup". I have followed that and done it during
one morning.

You should first verify that your serial connection works with getty. Connect an
ordinary PC with a null-modem cable. Run terminal emulation, see what you get.
It should be a Digital UNIX login prompt.

Then just install a ppp account, with pppd as shell and that's it. It worked
"out of the box" on my AlphaStation 200.

To be honest, I've had trouble. With serial I/O modules on AS 4100, not AS 200.
The earlier series had some crippled COM ports, fixed at 9600 baud and no modem
controll. Maybe that's bugging you.

Nix.





