In comp.unix.osf.osf1 Joshua Hart <hart@yomomma.med.nyu.edu> wrote:
: I have taken, as an experiment, the ZLXp-L2@5 graphics card out of my
: Digital Alpha Station 600 5/266, and put it into my Alpha server 2100A.

: Unfortunately the Alpha Server 2100A kernel does not include support for
: the card (ZLXp-L2@5). I did go back and remove, then reinstall O3D* from
: the layered products CD (v4.8).

: How do I go about compiling in support for this card?  It must be
: possible, it works just great on the Alpha Station 600.


In a similar situation we just copied the driver name from the kernel
configuration file of the machine where the card originated from into
that of the target machine. Here are examples from our /sys/conf/HOSTNAME files
for different graphics options.

ZLXp2-E Rev 34 card
controller      tga0       at pci0      slot  13

TRIO S3 card
controller      trio0      at pci0      slot  11

Powerstorm 4D50 (?)
controller      vga0       at pci0      slot  11

I don't really fully understand how to interpret the slot number info, 
but you might get away by making an educated guess 
from a comparison comparing the two old configuration files. 
Cross your fingers and rebuild the kernel. 

