Look at 
http://www.unix.digital.com/faqs/publications/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/HTML/AA-QTLGB-TE_html/CHPTR002.HTM#UPDATE-PATH-TABLE

Table 2-3: Successive Update Paths (to v4.0B)

  If you are currently using...
                               Update the operating system to..
  Version 3.2, 3.2A, or 3.2B 
                               Version 3.2C by using the installupdate command 
  Version 3.2C, 3.2D-1, or 3.2D-2 
                               Version 4.0 by using the installupdate command  
  Version 3.2E-1, 3.2E-2, or 3.2F 
                               Version 3.2G by using setld -l 
  Version 3.2G 
                               Version 4.0A by using the installupdate command 
  Version 4.0 or 4.0A 
                               Version 4.0B by using the installupdate command 

Additionally v4.0B to v4.0D with installupdate, but you _might_ go
from v4.0 or v4.0A directly to v4.0D also. I do not remember clearly.

Kjell



