We had exactly the same problem with a very array in a Fortran program.  The
issue is the default values for datasize limits in the kernel.  I increased it
to the 1GB maximum by inserting the line

	ulimit -d 1048576

into /etc/profile, and the line

	limit datasize 1048576 kbytes

into /etc/csh.login.  This ensures that each user gets the value set properly.

I'm sure that there is some kernel build parameter that would set the default
appropriately, but I've not got the time to track it down myself, and what I
have works.
