I knew that it was ok to put an ultra SCSI drive on a SCSI-2 controller and
that the ultra SCSI drive would just "down-grade" to the slower speed, but I
was under the impression that although you could put narrow devices on a wide
bus (which I believe reduces all traffic on that bus to "narrow"), I thought
that the converse (putting wide devices on a narrow bus) would not work.

