From: Emmanuel Choquet <ics@cica.fr>
Subject: Re: long time waiting on TELNET
Date: 1998/08/25
Message-ID: <35E28846.B9A33F64@cica.fr>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 384501250
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
References: <6rk7ms$ec9$1@goof.de.uu.net>
To: Anton Jaeger <anton@jaeger.m.eunet.de>
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: IC/S&C
Mime-Version: 1.0
Reply-To: ics@cica.fr
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

You probably have a DNS client on the Telnet server machine. In this case, it
allways tries
to reverse lookup the address of the telnet client. If your bind server(s)
cannot do it, it times out
after 2 minutes.

Solutions : -1- Declare your telnet clients in your bind servers
                -2- In the mean time, declare your telnet clients address in the
/etc/hosts file of the
telnet server and check in /etc/svc.conf that the local hosts file is checked
before bind. In this case the
reverse lookup will be local, and response time will be falshy.

Good luck,



