This sounds like Enhanced Security (C2) login module. That happens when you
don't have that X terminal (from which you're trying to log in) described in a
terminal database.

Versions prior to 4.0 held this database in an ASCII files
"/etc/auth/system/ttys & devassign". Versions 4.0 use binary forms of the same
files and should be accessed through proper utilities, like "edauth".

