Yeah, actually the "may not be needed" comment is more because I'm not
certain about the semantics of the builtin locking routines. If they
already do WMB/MB, then it's not needed. You'd really need to take a
look at the assembly code produced in a little more detail.

This, frankly, is why Digital should have provided & established
spinlocks, rather than insisting everyone use pthread mutex locks,
which have a lot of extra overhead. Sometimes portability is much less
important than performance.

