I've had numerous problems with AdvFS kernel panics too.  However, this
was when I was using the traditional storage method.  I've switched to
CNFS and all is going well.  I am using traditional files, not block
devices.  This gives me the possibility to migrate to a different set of
disks, which is one nice AdvFS feature I can't live without..

Anyway, AdvFS is a poor choice for any filesystem that uses a lot of
files.  The block size is something like 8k, plus every directory entry
and hard link takes that amount of space.  This is murder for a news
spool.

