FTP Administrator wrote:
> 
> Hello,
> 
> I'd like to know if it's possible to move an AdvFS composed by several
> disks to another
> machine and to have it alive again without to suffer data losses.
> 
> We have a machine suffered a major disk failure on the system disk
> (ufs), so we have to
> change it. How can save info about structure of a advfs domain
> containing some
> important data?

Well, forst of all, backups are a very good idea. Try booting from DU CD,
recreate AdvFS domain structure (/etc/fdmns/*) and back it up (vdump)

Now you can do three things.

1. Get a new machine, set it up, create AdvFS domain large enough for your
backed up file system and restore it (vrestore).

2. Take all good disks with that valid AdvFS domain on them, plug them into the
new machine, create system disk (actually, instal the OS from scratch), and just
configure the domain (/etc/fdmns/*).

3. Plug a new disk into the old machine and do the same as (2).

Nix.





