Currently we use ipc semaphores to sync access of different
processes to a shared memory region. This appears to be quite
slow. About 25-30% system time are required due to the system
calles made. 

Now we want to use mutex. (posix mutex) It does appear that
this can not be used easily for sync different processes on
shared memory (or mmap memory) For SUN-Solaris-2.5.1 it is
written in the manual to the pthread_mutex that it can be used
also for different processes via mmap or shared memory.
(not only for tasks within a process)

Is there something equal on OSF1 (DecUnix-4.0[abcd]) Important
is that no system call need to be made.

Regards,

