Jeff Denham <jdenham@brighttiger.com> writes:
> Sorry to disappoint on another front: a PSHARED implementation
> is probably going to make a system call when there's contention
> on the mutex. With no contention, the thread can lock and
> go, but with contention, it's probably going to block in the
> kernel, and that takes a system call.
--

But, in a 'mmap' region, you can also use the native spinlock/critical
section mechanisms. These will differ from machine to machine.

For the alpha, the easiest way to construct an atomic spinlock would
be to use the API provided in /usr/include/alpha/bulitins.h.

E.g., a lock acquire would be:

acquire(volatile int *addr)
{
	/* Spin, waiting for location to be available */
	for(;;) {
	  while (*addr != 0);
	  if ( __ATOMIC_EXCH_LONG(addr, 1) == 0 ) {
		break;
	  }
	 /* might not be needed, ya never know and
	    you're not doing much else right now anyway.. */
	  __MB();
	}
}

release(volatile int *addr)
{
	*addr = 0;
	__MB();
}

-- 
Dirk Grunwald                 Assoc. Prof, Univ. of Colorado at Boulder



