BINGO!  The silk-screening on the cards only indicate the PBXGA and various
other 50-# part numbers.  On the plate which maintains access to the monitor
resolution/freq. settings, the 3-tied 15 pin-D jack and the stereo jack (the
jack that looks like a mini-phone plug jack) is the PBXGA-*A/*N numbering.
The hardware is the same -- just the ordering number changes so that the NT
driver is shipped with the card.

BTW, I have several ZLXp-E1 cards if there's any interest.  What's the going
rate for these?  

